==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
{{compound|hard|wood|lang=en}}
===Alternative form===
* hard wood
===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{label|en|countable|mostly in botany and forestry}} The [[wood]] from any [[dicotyledon]]ous tree, without regard to its hardness.
#: {{ux|en|Balsa is a '''hardwood''', but a soft hardwood.}}
# {{label|en|countable}} (in more general use) As the preceding but limited to those that are commercial [[timber]]s, and are at least average in hardness.
#: {{ux|en|Ash, hickory and oak are some of the most prominent domestic '''hardwoods'''.}}
#*{{quote-book|year=1898|author={{w|Winston Churchill (novelist)|Winston Churchill}}
|title={{w|The Celebrity}}|chapter=10
|passage=Mr. Cooke had had a sloop yacht built at Far Harbor, the completion of which had been delayed, and which was but just delivered. […] The Maria had a cabin, which was finished in '''hard wood''' and yellow plush, and accommodations for keeping things cold.}}
# {{label|en|countable|forestry}} The tree or tree species that yields the preceding.
#: {{ux|en|This '''hardwood''' has been planted extensively throughout the hills here.}}
# {{label|en|uncountable}} A joint term for the commercial timbers, without distinguishing which.
#: {{ux|en|You should have used '''hardwood''' for this window sill instead of this junk.}}
# {{label|en|sports|slang}} The sport of basketball, in particular the basketball court.

